{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1002591-using-real-cities-as-game-locations","id":1002591,"title":"Using real cities as game locations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-13T12:05:43-08:00","id":1002591,"title":"Using real cities as game locations","content":"A while back, I was hoping to use the city of Vancouver as the setting for a game or two. It is huge and varied, allowing for most kinds of characters and scenarios, and it also has a huge place in my heart due to many visits with family. Unfortunately, Vancouver is also huge and varied, and I have no idea how to map such a city out for players to use and play within without copious usage of google maps. Any ideas on how to lessen the strain for this kind of setting without lessening the setting itself?<br /> <br /> Naturally, this applies to other cities, both larger and smaller than Vancouver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 11-13-2016, 03:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T12:35:18-08:00","id":1002606,"title":"","content":"I buy travel maps! I set a game in Montreal during a rebellion against a totalitarian government, and bought a laminated Quebec map from Barnes and Noble. One half street-by-street, one half general. Then, I got skinny-dry erase markers to circle where they were/needed to go, who controlled what city blocks, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T12:36:08-08:00","id":1002607,"title":"","content":"I found this one for you:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.barnesandnoble.com/w/streetwise-vancouver-map-laminated-city-center-street-map-of-vancouver-canada-folding-pocket-size-travel-map-with-metro-streetwise-maps/1015371653\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://prodimage.images-bn.com/pimages/9781734552553_p0_v2_s192x300.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.barnesandnoble.com/w/streetwise-vancouver-map-laminated-city-center-street-map-of-vancouver-canada-folding-pocket-size-travel-map-with-metro-streetwise-maps/1015371653\" target=\"_blank\"> BN No Results Page </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.barnesandnoble.com/w/streetwise-vancouver-map-laminated-city-center-street-map-of-vancouver-canada-folding-pocket-size-travel-map-with-metro-streetwise-maps/1015371653\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.barnesandnoble.com/w/streetwise-vancouver-map-laminated-city-center-street-map-of-vancouver-canada-folding-pocket-size-travel-map-with-metro-streetwise-maps/1015371653 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T13:13:33-08:00","id":1002620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1002591-using-real-cities-as-game-locations?p=1002606#post1002606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I buy travel maps! I set a game in Montreal during a rebellion against a totalitarian government, and bought a laminated Quebec map from Barnes and Noble. One half street-by-street, one half general. Then, I got skinny-dry erase markers to circle where they were/needed to go, who controlled what city blocks, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an excellent idea, and thank you for finding an appropriate map for it, it is very kind. It does hit a bit of a snag given that my games are all online (no local gaming group), but if nothing else it's a solid way to plan the area out, and if I needed to I could either scan them or find an online map and relocate the marked out areas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T13:20:45-08:00","id":1002622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1002591-using-real-cities-as-game-locations?p=1002620#post1002620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is an excellent idea, and thank you for finding an appropriate map for it, it is very kind. It does hit a bit of a snag given that my games are all online (no local gaming group), but if nothing else it's a solid way to plan the area out, and if I needed to I could either scan them or find an online map and relocate the marked out areas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I'm sorry, I didn't know they were online! I still think it's a good resource, though, for all of the reasons you said. Even if you have to send photos each time, you have one singular map you're marking and don't have to go back and forth to and from Google Maps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T13:31:31-08:00","id":1002625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1002591-using-real-cities-as-game-locations#post1002591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A while back, I was hoping to use the city of Vancouver as the setting for a game or two. It is huge and varied, allowing for most kinds of characters and scenarios, and it also has a huge place in my heart due to many visits with family. Unfortunately, Vancouver is also huge and varied, and I have no idea how to map such a city out for players to use and play within without copious usage of google maps. Any ideas on how to lessen the strain for this kind of setting without lessening the setting itself?<br /> <br /> Naturally, this applies to other cities, both larger and smaller than Vancouver.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have questions about Vancouver specifically, feel free to PM me. I'm a resident, and I wrote the Vancouver section that's in the <b>Beast</b> core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 11-13-2016, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T16:40:24-08:00","id":1002697,"title":"","content":"Aside asking for residents among forum's members, that is really a great way to begin (I did it once for a game in Rome), I suggest to use the internet during play without compunction. Don't ask how to do without Google Maps, <u>use</u> Google Maps. If you don't want to do it during game, make your research before and print what you need.<br /> <br /> I found that Ggle Maps and Wikipedia are excellent for quick reference during play. Doing research before to find other good sources, like the aforementioned residents, is also good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T17:52:57-08:00","id":1002722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1002591-using-real-cities-as-game-locations?p=1002622#post1002622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Oh, I'm sorry, I didn't know they were online! I still think it's a good resource, though, for all of the reasons you said. Even if you have to send photos each time, you have one singular map you're marking and don't have to go back and forth to and from Google Maps.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries, it was my mistake. I should have specified that in my original post. Now the only hurtle is finding a local Barnes and Noble, though purchasing online is definitely an option. Something I should probably exercise more, too...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1002591-using-real-cities-as-game-locations?p=1002625#post1002625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you have questions about Vancouver specifically, feel free to PM me. I'm a resident, and I wrote the Vancouver section that's in the <b>Beast</b> core.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, I really enjoyed that section. I loved the lore evoked, and the idea that something has broken part of the Primordial Dream in a way that, while advantageous is something nobody can figure out is interesting. It opens the door for other portions of the world having similarly unique problems (as much a paradox as that is), and the abuse that would ensue from them. Thank you for choosing Vancouver for it, however dour it makes my home away from home.<br /> <br /> If I can think of any particular questions, I shall definitely ask (I'm a bit sad to say that I've not internalized the areas very well). Thank you for the offer. :-)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1002591-using-real-cities-as-game-locations?p=1002697#post1002697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Aside asking for residents among forum's members, that is really a great way to begin (I did it once for a game in Rome), I suggest to use the internet during play without compunction. Don't ask how to do without Google Maps, <u>use</u> Google Maps. If you don't want to do it during game, make your research before and print what you need.<br /> <br /> I found that Ggle Maps and Wikipedia are excellent for quick reference during play. Doing research before to find other good sources, like the aforementioned residents, is also good.</div> </div> </div> </div>That really is a fair point. The only reason I specified for ways around Google Maps is because of how fiddly the interface can be, and I wasn't sure if I was looking at the right resource for what I wanted to do. Sometimes I miss some very obvious solutions. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T04:50:25-08:00","id":1002832,"title":"","content":"I'm running a Promethean game set in Detroit, I use google maps. You can save points of interest, add them, and rename them. I then copied the play area map to add territories and other data overlays","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T16:22:11-08:00","id":1003124,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2861_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2861\" data-vbnamecard=\"2861\">Nyx</a> Another fact I'd overlooked! Thank you for informing me about this. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}